<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schaan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schaan is the largest municipality of Liechtenstein, just north of the capital Vaduz on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> plain. An ancient settlement with Roman remains, it became the country's main industrial centre in the twentieth century, home to the construction-tool maker Hilti, founded there in 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schaan.jpg" alt="Schaan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michielverbeek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schaan,_die_Pfarrkirche_Sankt_Laurentius_in_straatzicht_foto7_2014-07-21_10.12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
